Query 1: Process memory (corrected)
timeseries mem = avg(dt.process.memory.working_set_size),
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}
| fieldsAdd `Memory (GiB)` = round(arrayAvg(mem) / 1073741824, decimals:2)
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance
    | fieldsAdd hostId = belongs_to[dt.entity.host]
    | fields id, Process = entity.name, hostId, tags
    | expand tag = tags
    | filter contains(tag, "APMID:") or contains(tag, "APPID:") or contains(tag, "APPName:")
    | summarize apmids   = arrayRemoveNulls(collectDistinct(
                              if(contains(tag, "APMID:"), splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1],
                              else: if(contains(tag, "APPID:"), splitString(tag, "APPID:")[1])))),
                appNames = arrayRemoveNulls(collectDistinct(
                              if(contains(tag, "APPName:"), splitString(tag, "APPName:")[1]))),
                by:{id, Process, hostId}
    | filter arraySize(apmids) == 1
    | fieldsAdd apmid = apmids[0], AppName = coalesce(appNames[0], apmids[0])
    | filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
    | fields id, Process, hostId, AppName
  ], sourceField:dt.entity.process_group_instance, lookupField:id, prefix:"p."
| filter isNotNull(p.id)
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.host | fields id, Host = entity.name ],
         sourceField:p.hostId, lookupField:id, prefix:"h."
| fields `App Name` = p.AppName, Process = p.Process, Host = h.Host, `Memory (GiB)`, dt.entity.process_group_instance
| sort `Memory (GiB)` desc
| limit 10


If you want a true utilization %: swap the metric to dt.process.memory.usage and delete the / 1073741824 conversion. I haven't confirmed its unit, so open it in the metric browser and check that it says percent, as you did for uptime. Then name the column Memory (%).

Query 2: Slowest services (corrected)
timeseries rt = avg(dt.service.request.response_time),
           by:{dt.entity.service}
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.service
    | fields id, Service = entity.name, serviceType, tags
    | filter in(serviceType, {"WEB_REQUEST_SERVICE", "WEB_SERVICE"})
    | expand tag = tags
    | filter contains(tag, "APMID:") or contains(tag, "APPID:") or contains(tag, "APPName:")
    | summarize apmids   = arrayRemoveNulls(collectDistinct(
                              if(contains(tag, "APMID:"), splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1],
                              else: if(contains(tag, "APPID:"), splitString(tag, "APPID:")[1])))),
                appNames = arrayRemoveNulls(collectDistinct(
                              if(contains(tag, "APPName:"), splitString(tag, "APPName:")[1]))),
                by:{id, Service}
    | filter arraySize(apmids) == 1
    | fieldsAdd apmid = apmids[0], AppName = coalesce(appNames[0], apmids[0])
    | filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
    | fields id, Service, AppName
  ], sourceField:dt.entity.service, lookupField:id, prefix:"s."
| filter isNotNull(s.id)
| fieldsAdd `Response Time (ms)` = rt[] / 1000,
            rt_avg = arrayAvg(rt)
| fieldsAdd Series = concat(s.AppName, " | ", s.Service)
| sort rt_avg desc
| limit 10
| fields timeframe, interval, Series, `Response Time (ms)`, dt.entity.service


Two things to know:

This is a "top 10 slowest" view, not an exception list. It will always show 10 lines, even when everything is fast.
The average hides slow tails, and the metric is a histogram. If you want the tail, try percentile(dt.service.request.response_time, 90) in place of avg(...). I haven't tested that on your tenant.
